    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Travancore's victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-colachel">Battle of Colachel</a> in 1741 is considered the earliest example of an organised Asian power overcoming European military technology and tactics.</li><li>On 3 January 1750 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthanda-varma">Marthanda Varma</a> dedicated the kingdom to the deity Padmanabha, and its rulers thereafter governed as Padmanabha-dasar, servants of Padmanabha.</li><li>Treaties of 1788, 1795 and 1805 placed Travancore under British dominance; after Velu Thampi's rebellion of 1809 almost all its forces were disbanded and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> undertook its defence.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Chithira Thirunal's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-entry-proclamation">Temple Entry Proclamation</a> of 12 November 1936 opened every <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temple in Travancore to the backward communities and won praise from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swami-vivekananda">Swami Vivekananda</a> had earlier called the state &quot;The Lunatic Asylum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>&quot; for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> discrimination.</p></aside>
    </section>

